WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.958
- If you came to my house,
we wouldn't have mashed potatoes.

00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:06.958
- I bestow the pardon on Mr. Jon Gruden,
yes, I will.

00:00:06.958 --> 00:00:11.042
- Thank God you gave
$71 million to Alex Smith.

00:00:11.042 --> 00:00:15.292
♪♪♪

00:00:15.292 --> 00:00:17.375
- What up, everybody?
Welcome to "Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:19.583
It is the wonderful
Thanksgiving edition.

00:00:19.583 --> 00:00:22.167
Simms, you're practically family
at this point.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.125
- Oh, Happy Thanksgiving, Lefkoe.
- What did you bring?

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:25.917
- I brought nothing.
- Awesome.

00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:27.583
I brought the turkey.
- Oh, that's great.

00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:29.167
I'm not eating it.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.333
- Are you a leg or a wing guy?
- Uh, I'm a breast guy.

00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:32.667
- OK.
- A leg and a wing is

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.125
the same thing, but—
- No, it's not.

00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:35.667
The leg is that,
and the wing is that.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:36.958
- I mean, they're
basically the same piece of meat.

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:38.167
- It's white meat and dark meat.

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.000
- Is it, really?

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.875
- This is a meaningless debate
that we will figure out later.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.625
But right now it is time
to do our pardons.

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:45.000
You've seen presidential pardons
where they forgive the turkey

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.583
You've seen presidential pardons
where they forgive the turkey

00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:49.417
and let it live another day.

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:52.875
We have some people in the NFL
that may need to be pardoned.

00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:58.042
First one up—
oh, look at this turkey.

00:00:58.042 --> 00:00:59.875
Jon Gruden.
- Oh!

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:03.667
-Are you willing to pardon Jon
Gruden for trading Khalil Mack

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.917
and leading to what we're seeing
right now in Oakland?

00:01:05.917 --> 00:01:08.708
- I bestow the pardon
on Mr. Jon Gruden.

00:01:08.708 --> 00:01:10.167
- Wow.
- Yes, I will.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.833
I will give him the pardon
because I think

00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:14.542
there was more in play
with the Khalil Mack situation

00:01:14.542 --> 00:01:16.000
than what we know.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.500
I do think there was
some financial issues.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.667
- The whole story
hasn't come out yet.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.333
- It has not all come out.

00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:21.833
- Mark Davis' checks are
bouncing, is what you're saying.

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:23.583
- Exactly right.
Well, he's had a few issues.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.667
We know that, but I'm giving him
the pardon for Khalil Mack.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.167
- OK. Man, he's so
good, Khalil Mack.
- Yeah.

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.375
- It's hard to give him
that pardon.

00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:30.833
We got a double turkey here—
- Oh gosh.

00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:32.875
- So you can pardon one,
you can pardon both.

00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:36.042
On the right, Ty Montgomery,
his fumble in the Rams game.

00:01:36.042 --> 00:01:39.167
Mike McCarthy, punting
4th-and-2 against the Seahawks.

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:42.417
Both of these turkeys
prevented us from seeing Rodgers

00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:44.000
possibly going the length
of the field.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.167
- Cook 'em.
Well-done.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:46.958
- Both of 'em?
- Both of 'em.

00:01:46.958 --> 00:01:49.042
I mean, put one in the fryer
and the other one in the oven

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:50.292
and make sure they're well-done.
Yeah, they're cooked.

00:01:50.292 --> 00:01:51.792
- Just keep 'em juicy.

00:01:51.792 --> 00:01:53.500
- There's no excuse
for Ty Montgomery bringing

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.750
the ball out in that situation
and cheating all of us

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.333
including his own team,
the Packers

00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:59.458
and not giving Aaron Rodgers
a chance to win it.

00:01:59.458 --> 00:02:01.083
And then Mike McCarthy

00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:04.792
with two of your best
defensive players not healthy—

00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:07.375
- And you just let up drives
of 77 and 75 yards.

00:02:07.375 --> 00:02:09.083
- And you think now
you're gonna stop them?
- Yeah.

00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:10.667
- No, sorry.
Into the fryer.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.125
- I got one more for you.

00:02:12.125 --> 00:02:16.125
- OK.
- This is Week 2—

00:02:16.125 --> 00:02:18.458
- Ooh.
- When, after the Jaguars
beat the Patriots—

00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:21.000
I have a clip for this turkey.
- Oh, thank you.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.250
- Chalk it up.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.708
They're gonna win the Super Bowl.
- [Laughing]

00:02:23.708 --> 00:02:25.792
- That was you talking
about the Jaguars

00:02:25.792 --> 00:02:27.667
with their win
over the Patriots.
- Ohhh.

00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:30.250
I am going to say,
in your defense—

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.125
- Yeah?
- I'm gonna pardon this turkey.

00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:35.708
One, because "Blank &amp; Lefkoe"
doesn't have a cachet to it.

00:02:35.708 --> 00:02:37.333
- OK, thank you.
- But I'll be honest.

00:02:37.333 --> 00:02:39.333
When the Jaguars beat the crap
